# ══════════════ Customer identity documents — never commit ══════════════
#
# PWD / Senior Citizen ID images uploaded at checkout. These are other
# people's identity documents: they must live on the server only, never in
# version control, and never in a repository's history where removing them
# later requires rewriting every teammate's clone.
#
# The five files currently sitting in public/uploads/ids/ turned out to be
# test uploads rather than real customers' IDs (see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §7a),
# but that is luck, not a control. In production this directory is exactly
# where real scans land, so it is excluded outright.
#
# The local files are deliberately left on disk — the app serves whatever is
# there — they are simply never tracked.
/public/uploads/ids/
/storage/app/public/discount_ids/

# Environment files of every shape. `.env` alone does not match .env.local
# or a dated copy someone made before editing, and those leak exactly the
# same database and mail credentials.
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example
